The [[Eisenhower matrix|https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_management#The_Eisenhower_Method]]
(also known as the ''urgent-important matrix'') is a [[dashboard|$:/plugins/nico/projectify/doc/Dashboard]]
tab that helps you decide what to work on first. It acts as a kanban board
displaying all your open tasks in four quadrants, based on how urgent and how
important they are:

* ''Do first'' - important & urgent
* ''Schedule'' - important, but not urgent
* ''Delegate'' - urgent, but not important
* ''Eliminate'' - neither important nor urgent

Every todo is classified into one of the four quadrants, just like its priority:
the quadrant is a property of the todo that you can change at any time. Todos
created without an explicit quadrant default to ''Eliminate'' (neither important
nor urgent).

You can change the quadrant of a todo with the quadrant button displayed next to
it, or simply [[drag & drop|https://tiddlywiki.com/#Drag%20and%20Drop]] it from
one quadrant to another in the board. The board updates dynamically, so a todo
immediately moves to the quadrant matching its current state.

<<py-tip "The quadrant of a task is stored in its `quadrant` field (`do`, `schedule`, `delegate` or `eliminate`), which can be used in filters (for example `[tag[todo]quadrant[do]]`).">>